{"title": "The Ice Cream Truck", "text": "On a hot afternoon, Nina hears music on her street. It is the ice cream truck! She runs to ask Mom for money. Mom gives her two dollars. Nina picks a strawberry cone. It starts to melt fast in the sun. Nina licks it quickly. Pink drips land on her shirt, but she does not mind.", "q": ["T|It is a hot afternoon.", "F|Nina hears a bell.", "T|Nina asks Mom for money.", "F|Mom gives her five dollars.", "T|Nina picks strawberry.", "F|The cone stays cold and hard.", "T|Pink drips land on her shirt.", "F|Nina is upset about her shirt.", "T|The ice cream truck plays music.", "C|What does Nina hear?|music*|thunder|a dog", "C|How much money does Mom give?|two dollars*|one dollar|ten dollars", "C|What flavour does Nina pick?|strawberry*|chocolate|vanilla", "C|What does the ice cream do?|melts fast*|freezes|falls down", "C|How does Nina lick it?|quickly*|slowly|not at all", "C|Where do the drips land?|on her shirt*|on her shoes|on the dog", "C|What colour are the drips?|pink*|brown|white", "C|Who gives Nina money?|Mom*|Dad|a friend", "C|How does Nina feel about the drips?|she does not mind*|she cries|she is angry", "B|Nina hears ____ on her street.|music", "B|It is the ice cream ____!|truck", "B|Mom gives her two ____.|dollars", "B|Nina picks a strawberry ____.|cone", "B|It starts to ____ fast.|melt", "B|Nina licks it ____.|quickly", "B|Drips land on her ____.|shirt"]},
{"title": "The Class Hamster", "text": "Our class has a hamster named Peanut. He is small and brown. Peanut runs on his wheel all night. In the day, he sleeps in a pile of paper. On Friday, Lucas takes Peanut home for the weekend. He gives him fresh water and seeds. On Monday, Peanut comes back to class, safe and happy.", "q": ["T|The hamster is named Peanut.", "F|Peanut is big and white.", "T|Peanut runs on his wheel.", "F|Peanut runs all day.", "T|Peanut sleeps in paper.", "F|Lucas takes Peanut home on Monday.", "T|Lucas gives him seeds.", "F|Peanut stays at Lucas’s house.", "T|Peanut comes back on Monday.", "C|What is the hamster’s name?|Peanut*|Coco|Max", "C|What colour is Peanut?|brown*|white|black", "C|When does Peanut run?|all night*|all day|never", "C|Where does he sleep?|in a pile of paper*|in a box|on a bed", "C|Who takes him home?|Lucas*|the teacher|Maya", "C|When does Lucas take him?|on Friday*|on Monday|on Tuesday", "C|What does Lucas give him?|water and seeds*|milk and bread|candy", "C|How is Peanut on Monday?|safe and happy*|sick|lost", "C|How big is Peanut?|small*|huge|tall", "B|Our class has a ____.|hamster", "B|He is small and ____.|brown", "B|Peanut runs on his ____.|wheel", "B|In the day, he ____.|sleeps", "B|Lucas takes him home for the ____.|weekend", "B|He gives him fresh ____.|water", "B|On ____, Peanut comes back.|Monday"]},
{"title": "Rainbow After Rain", "text": "The rain stops and the sun comes out. Eva looks at the sky. She sees a rainbow! It has red, orange, yellow, green, blue and purple. Eva calls her little brother to come and see. They count the colours together. Soon the rainbow fades away. Eva draws it so she can keep it forever.", "q": ["T|The rain stops.", "F|Eva sees a cloud shaped like a cat.", "T|Eva sees a rainbow.", "F|The rainbow has no green.", "T|Eva calls her little brother.", "F|They count trees.", "T|The rainbow fades away.", "F|Eva takes a photo.", "T|Eva draws the rainbow.", "C|What comes out after the rain?|the sun*|the moon|the stars", "C|What does Eva see?|a rainbow*|a bird|a plane", "C|Who does Eva call?|her little brother*|her mom|her friend", "C|What do they count?|the colours*|the clouds|the cars", "C|What happens to the rainbow?|it fades away*|it gets bigger|it falls", "C|How does Eva keep it?|she draws it*|she paints the sky|she catches it", "C|Which colour is in the rainbow?|purple*|pink|brown", "C|Where does Eva look?|at the sky*|at the ground|at a book", "C|How long will Eva keep it?|forever*|one day|one hour", "B|The rain ____.|stops", "B|The sun comes ____.|out", "B|She sees a ____!|rainbow", "B|They count the ____ together.|colours", "B|Soon the rainbow fades ____.|away", "B|Eva ____ it.|draws", "B|She can keep it ____.|forever"]}
