{"title": "The Lost Mitten", "text": "On a cold morning in Winnipeg, Kwame walked to school with his friend Sara. When he got to class, he saw that one red mitten was missing. Kwame felt worried because his grandma had knit the mittens for him. At recess, Sara helped him look. They checked the snowbank by the fence and the path by the slide. Then Sara spotted something red under the bench. It was the mitten! It was wet, so the teacher put it on the heater to dry. After lunch, Kwame’s mitten was warm and dry again.", "q": ["T|Kwame walked to school with Sara.", "F|Kwame lost a blue mitten.", "T|Grandma knit the mittens.", "F|Sara laughed at Kwame.", "T|They looked at recess.", "F|The mitten was in the classroom.", "T|The mitten was wet.", "F|The mitten was still wet after lunch.", "C|What city is the story in?|Winnipeg*|Halifax|Toronto", "C|What colour was the mitten?|blue|red*|green", "C|How did Kwame feel?|worried*|silly|sleepy", "C|Who knit the mittens?|his mom|his grandma*|his aunt", "C|When did they look?|at recess*|at night|before school", "C|Where was the mitten?|under the bench*|by the slide|in a tree", "C|Who found the mitten?|Kwame|the teacher|Sara*", "C|Where did the teacher put it?|on the heater*|in a bag|on a hook", "C|What was the weather like?|hot|rainy|cold*", "C|How was the mitten after lunch?|lost|warm and dry*|torn", "B|One red ____ was missing.|mitten", "B|Sara helped him ____.|look", "B|They checked the ____ by the fence.|snowbank", "B|Sara spotted something red under the ____.|bench", "B|The teacher put it on the ____ to dry.|heater", "B|Find a word in the story that rhymes with “bold”: ____|cold", "B|After ____, the mitten was warm and dry.|lunch"]},
{"title": "A Trip to the Library", "text": "Every Saturday, Mateo and his mom take the bus to the library in Ottawa. Mateo loves books about animals. This week, he found a book about beavers. He learned that beavers build dams with sticks and mud. He also learned that a beaver’s teeth never stop growing! The librarian, Ms. Chen, showed him a book about owls too. Mateo took both books home. That night, he read the beaver book to his little sister, Luz. She liked the picture of the baby beavers best.", "q": ["T|Mateo goes to the library on Saturday.", "F|Mateo walks to the library.", "T|Mateo loves books about animals.", "F|Mateo found a book about bears.", "T|Beavers build dams with sticks and mud.", "F|A beaver’s teeth stop growing.", "T|Ms. Chen is the librarian.", "F|Mateo took one book home.", "C|Who goes with Mateo?|his dad|his mom*|his friend", "C|How do they get there?|by car|by bike|by bus*", "C|What city is the library in?|Ottawa*|Regina|Victoria", "C|What kind of books does Mateo love?|animal books*|joke books|car books", "C|What do beavers build?|nests|dams*|caves", "C|What never stops growing?|a beaver’s tail|a beaver’s teeth*|a beaver’s fur", "C|Ms. Chen showed him a book about …|owls*|fish|trains", "C|Who is Luz?|his cousin|his sister*|his friend", "C|When did Mateo read to Luz?|that night*|that morning|at school", "C|What did Luz like best?|the baby beavers*|the owls|the dam", "B|Mateo loves books about ____.|animals", "B|Beavers build dams with sticks and ____.|mud", "B|The ____ showed him a book about owls.|librarian", "B|Mateo took both ____ home.|books", "B|He read the beaver book to his little ____.|sister", "B|Find a word in the story that rhymes with “hat”: ____|that", "B|She liked the ____ of the baby beavers best.|picture"]},
{"title": "The Class Pumpkin", "text": "In October, Ms. Okafor’s class in Moncton grew a pumpkin on the windowsill. First, they planted a seed in a pot of soil. Each day, Hana checked if it needed water. After two weeks, a green vine curled out of the pot. Soon a little yellow flower opened. The flower turned into a tiny green pumpkin. The class measured it every Friday. By the end of the month, the pumpkin was orange and as big as a baseball. The class named it Pip.", "q": ["T|The class grew a pumpkin.", "F|The pumpkin grew outside.", "T|They planted a seed in soil.", "F|Leo checked the water each day.", "T|A green vine curled out of the pot.", "F|The flower was red.", "T|They measured it every Friday.", "F|The pumpkin got as big as a car.", "C|When did the class grow the pumpkin?|in October*|in June|in March", "C|Whose class is it?|Ms. Okafor’s*|Mr. Lee’s|Ms. Roy’s", "C|Where did the pumpkin grow?|on the windowsill*|in the gym|in a field", "C|Who checked the water?|Hana*|Ms. Okafor|Pip", "C|What came out after two weeks?|a vine*|a bug|a leaf", "C|What colour was the flower?|white|pink|yellow*", "C|What did the flower turn into?|a seed|a tiny pumpkin*|an apple", "C|How often did they measure it?|every Friday*|every hour|once", "C|How big did it get?|like a baseball*|like a house|like a bean", "C|What did they name the pumpkin?|Pip*|Pat|Pom", "B|They planted a seed in a pot of ____.|soil", "B|Each day, Hana checked if it needed ____.|water", "B|A green ____ curled out of the pot.|vine", "B|Soon a little yellow ____ opened.|flower", "B|By the end of the month, the pumpkin was ____.|orange", "B|Find a word in the story that rhymes with “say”: ____|day", "B|The class ____ it Pip.|named"]},
{"title": "The Hockey Game", "text": "On Saturday, Ethan and his dad went to a hockey game in Edmonton. The arena was loud and full of fans in orange shirts. Ethan ate popcorn and waved a big foam finger. In the third period, the home team scored the winning goal. Everyone jumped up and cheered. On the way home, Ethan said he wants to play hockey one day.", "q": ["T|Ethan went with his dad.", "F|The game was in Calgary.", "T|The fans wore orange shirts.", "F|Ethan ate a hot dog.", "T|Ethan waved a foam finger.", "F|The winning goal was in the first period.", "T|Everyone cheered.", "F|Ethan wants to be a referee.", "C|When did they go?|on Saturday*|on Monday|on Friday", "C|Where was the game?|Edmonton*|Toronto|Regina", "C|How was the arena?|loud and full*|quiet and empty|cold and dark", "C|What colour were the shirts?|orange*|blue|green", "C|What did Ethan eat?|popcorn*|pizza|ice cream", "C|What did Ethan wave?|a foam finger*|a flag|a scarf", "C|When was the winning goal?|in the third period*|in the first period|after the game", "C|What did everyone do?|jumped and cheered*|left early|sat quietly", "C|What does Ethan want to do?|play hockey*|sell popcorn|drive a bus", "C|Who scored the winning goal?|the home team*|the other team|Ethan", "B|The arena was loud and full of ____.|fans", "B|Ethan ate ____.|popcorn", "B|He waved a big foam ____.|finger", "B|The home team ____ the winning goal.|scored", "B|Everyone jumped up and ____.|cheered", "B|They went to a hockey ____.|game", "B|Ethan wants to play ____ one day.|hockey"]},
{"title": "The Missing Library Book", "text": "Aisha could not find her library book, The Lost Moose. It was due back on Friday. She looked under her bed, in her desk, and in the car. Then she remembered reading it to her little brother at bedtime. She checked his room and found the book under his pillow! Aisha returned it to the library just in time.", "q": ["T|The book is called The Lost Moose.", "F|The book was due on Monday.", "T|Aisha looked under her bed.", "F|Aisha looked in the garage.", "T|Aisha read to her brother.", "F|The book was in the fridge.", "T|The book was under a pillow.", "F|Aisha returned the book late.", "C|What was the book called?|The Lost Moose*|The Big Bear|The Red Fox", "C|When was it due?|on Friday*|on Sunday|on Tuesday", "C|Where did Aisha look first?|under her bed*|in the yard|at school", "C|What did she remember?|reading to her brother*|lending it to a friend|leaving it at school", "C|When did she read to him?|at bedtime*|at breakfast|at lunch", "C|Whose room did she check?|her brother’s*|her mom’s|her own", "C|Where was the book?|under his pillow*|on a shelf|in a bag", "C|When did she return it?|just in time*|a week late|never", "C|Who is younger?|her brother*|Aisha|her mom", "C|What did Aisha feel at first?|worried*|bored|silly", "B|Aisha could not find her library ____.|book", "B|It was due back on ____.|Friday", "B|She looked in her ____.|desk", "B|She read it at ____.|bedtime", "B|She found the book under his ____.|pillow", "B|She ____ it to the library.|returned", "B|She checked his ____.|room"]},
{"title": "The Butterfly Garden", "text": "In May, Mr. Patel’s class got five tiny caterpillars in a net home. The students fed them milkweed leaves. The caterpillars ate and grew bigger every day. Then each one made a hard shell called a chrysalis. After two weeks, beautiful monarch butterflies came out. On a sunny day, the class let them go in the school garden.", "q": ["T|The class got five caterpillars.", "F|They fed them lettuce.", "T|The caterpillars grew every day.", "F|The shell is called a cocoon in the story.", "T|Monarch butterflies came out.", "F|The butterflies came out after two days.", "T|The class let them go.", "F|They let them go on a rainy day.", "C|Who is the teacher?|Mr. Patel*|Ms. Lee|Mr. Brown", "C|When did they get the caterpillars?|in May*|in October|in January", "C|How many caterpillars?|five*|two|ten", "C|What did they eat?|milkweed leaves*|grass|apples", "C|What did each make?|a chrysalis*|a nest|a web", "C|How long until butterflies came out?|two weeks*|two days|two months", "C|What kind of butterflies?|monarch*|white|blue", "C|Where did they let them go?|the school garden*|the gym|the bus", "C|What was the weather?|sunny*|rainy|snowy", "C|Where did the caterpillars live?|in a net home*|in a fish tank|in a box", "B|They got tiny ____.|caterpillars", "B|The students fed them milkweed ____.|leaves", "B|They grew ____ every day.|bigger", "B|Each made a hard shell called a ____.|chrysalis", "B|Beautiful ____ butterflies came out.|monarch", "B|The class let them ____.|go", "B|They let them go in the school ____.|garden"]},
{"title": "Moving Day for Kenji", "text": "Kenji’s family moved to a new apartment in Montreal. Kenji felt nervous because he did not know anyone. On the first day, a girl named Julie knocked on the door. She lived next door and spoke French and English. She showed Kenji the park across the street. By dinner time, Kenji had a new friend and was not nervous anymore.", "q": ["T|Kenji moved to Montreal.", "F|They moved into a house.", "T|Kenji felt nervous.", "F|Julie lived far away.", "T|Julie spoke French and English.", "F|Julie showed him the school.", "T|The park was across the street.", "F|Kenji was still nervous at dinner.", "C|Where did Kenji move?|Montreal*|Halifax|Winnipeg", "C|What did they move into?|an apartment*|a farm|a boat", "C|Why was Kenji nervous?|he did not know anyone*|he was sick|he was late", "C|Who knocked on the door?|Julie*|the mail carrier|Kenji’s aunt", "C|Where did Julie live?|next door*|across town|upstairs", "C|What languages did Julie speak?|French and English*|Spanish|Japanese", "C|What did Julie show Kenji?|the park*|the store|the library", "C|Where was the park?|across the street*|far away|behind the school", "C|What did Kenji have by dinner?|a new friend*|a new bike|a new pet", "C|When did Julie come?|on the first day*|after a week|at night", "B|Kenji’s family moved to a new ____.|apartment", "B|Kenji felt ____.|nervous", "B|A girl named ____ knocked.|Julie", "B|She lived next ____.|door", "B|She showed Kenji the ____.|park", "B|Kenji had a new ____.|friend", "B|The park was across the ____.|street"]},
{"title": "Making Maple Taffy", "text": "In March, Chloé’s grandmother made maple taffy in the yard. First, she heated maple syrup on the stove until it was very hot and thick. Then she poured long lines of syrup onto clean snow. The syrup cooled and got sticky. Chloé rolled it up on a wooden stick. It was sweet and chewy, and her fingers got very sticky!", "q": ["T|The taffy was made in March.", "F|Chloé’s grandfather made the taffy.", "T|The syrup was heated on the stove.", "F|The syrup was poured on ice cubes.", "T|The syrup got sticky.", "F|Chloé used a metal spoon.", "T|The taffy was chewy.", "F|Chloé’s fingers stayed clean.", "C|When did they make taffy?|in March*|in July|in October", "C|Who made the taffy?|her grandmother*|her dad|her teacher", "C|What was heated?|maple syrup*|milk|chocolate", "C|How did the syrup get?|hot and thick*|cold and thin|frozen", "C|Where was it poured?|onto clean snow*|into a cup|on a plate", "C|What happened when it cooled?|it got sticky*|it melted|it turned blue", "C|What did Chloé roll it on?|a wooden stick*|a fork|a straw", "C|How did it taste?|sweet and chewy*|salty|sour", "C|What got sticky?|her fingers*|her shoes|the dog", "C|Where did they make it?|in the yard*|at school|at a store", "B|She heated maple ____.|syrup", "B|It became very hot and ____.|thick", "B|She poured it onto clean ____.|snow", "B|The syrup cooled and got ____.|sticky", "B|Chloé rolled it on a wooden ____.|stick", "B|It was sweet and ____.|chewy", "B|Her ____ got very sticky!|fingers"]},
{"title": "The Sandcastle Contest", "text": "At the beach in Prince Edward Island, there was a sandcastle contest. Leo and his cousin Mira built a castle with four towers and a moat. They used shells for windows and seaweed for flags. A wave almost washed the moat away, so they built a wall of sand. The judges gave them a blue ribbon for the best design.", "q": ["T|The beach was in Prince Edward Island.", "F|Leo worked with his brother.", "T|The castle had four towers.", "F|They used rocks for windows.", "T|They used seaweed for flags.", "F|A dog knocked the castle down.", "T|They built a wall of sand.", "F|They won a red ribbon.", "C|Where was the beach?|Prince Edward Island*|Vancouver|Ottawa", "C|Who helped Leo?|his cousin Mira*|his dad|his friend Sam", "C|How many towers?|four*|two|six", "C|What was around the castle?|a moat*|a fence|a road", "C|What were the windows made of?|shells*|leaves|sticks", "C|What were the flags made of?|seaweed*|paper|cloth", "C|What almost washed the moat away?|a wave*|the rain|a bucket", "C|What did they build to stop it?|a wall of sand*|a bridge|a tunnel", "C|What did they win?|a blue ribbon*|a trophy|a medal", "C|What was the prize for?|the best design*|the tallest castle|the fastest", "B|There was a sandcastle ____.|contest", "B|They built four ____.|towers", "B|They used ____ for windows.|shells", "B|A ____ almost washed the moat away.|wave", "B|They built a wall of ____.|sand", "B|The judges gave them a blue ____.|ribbon", "B|Leo built it with his cousin ____.|Mira"]},
{"title": "The School Concert", "text": "Every December, Hill Street School holds a winter concert. This year, Sana’s class sang a song about snowflakes. Sana played the triangle at the end of each verse. She practised every night so she would not miss a beat. On the big night, the gym was full of parents. When the song ended, Sana’s grandpa clapped the loudest of all.", "q": ["T|The concert is in December.", "F|The concert is in the library.", "T|The song was about snowflakes.", "F|Sana played the drum.", "T|Sana practised every night.", "F|The gym was empty.", "T|Parents came to the concert.", "F|Sana’s aunt clapped the loudest.", "C|When is the concert?|December*|June|April", "C|What is the school called?|Hill Street School*|Lake School|Pine School", "C|What was the song about?|snowflakes*|rain|birds", "C|What did Sana play?|the triangle*|the piano|the flute", "C|When did she play it?|at the end of each verse*|at the start|the whole time", "C|Why did she practise?|so she would not miss a beat*|to get candy|to sing louder", "C|Where was the concert?|in the gym*|outside|at a church", "C|Who filled the gym?|parents*|dogs|teachers only", "C|Who clapped the loudest?|her grandpa*|her mom|her teacher", "C|What season is the concert?|winter*|summer|spring", "B|The school holds a winter ____.|concert", "B|The song was about ____.|snowflakes", "B|Sana played the ____.|triangle", "B|She practised every ____.|night", "B|The gym was full of ____.|parents", "B|Her grandpa clapped the ____.|loudest", "B|She did not want to miss a ____.|beat"]},
{"title": "The Bird Feeder", "text": "Mateo and his mom made a bird feeder from an old milk carton. They cut a window in the side and filled it with seeds. Then they hung it from a branch outside the kitchen window. The next morning, a bright red cardinal came to eat. Later, three chickadees and a blue jay visited. Mateo kept a list of every bird he saw.", "q": ["T|They used an old milk carton.", "F|They used a tin can.", "T|They filled it with seeds.", "F|They hung it on the porch.", "T|A cardinal came first.", "F|The cardinal was yellow.", "T|A blue jay visited.", "F|Mateo took photos of every bird.", "C|Who helped Mateo?|his mom*|his dad|his sister", "C|What was the feeder made from?|a milk carton*|a shoe box|a bucket", "C|What did they cut?|a window*|a door|a hole in the roof", "C|What did they fill it with?|seeds*|bread|fruit", "C|Where did they hang it?|from a branch*|on a fence|in the garage", "C|Which bird came first?|a cardinal*|a robin|a crow", "C|What colour was the cardinal?|red*|blue|brown", "C|How many chickadees came?|three*|one|five", "C|What did Mateo keep?|a list of birds*|a feather|a nest", "C|When did the first bird come?|the next morning*|that night|a week later", "B|They made a bird ____.|feeder", "B|They filled it with ____.|seeds", "B|They hung it from a ____.|branch", "B|A bright red ____ came.|cardinal", "B|Three ____ visited.|chickadees", "B|A blue ____ visited.|jay", "B|Mateo kept a ____ of birds.|list"]},
{"title": "Camping Under the Stars", "text": "In August, Hana’s family went camping at a lake. They set up a green tent and gathered sticks for a fire. Dad showed Hana how to roast a marshmallow without burning it. At night, they lay on a blanket and looked up at the sky. Hana saw a shooting star and made a wish. She did not tell anyone what she wished for.", "q": ["T|They went camping in August.", "F|They camped by the ocean.", "T|The tent was green.", "F|They gathered rocks for a fire.", "T|Dad showed Hana how to roast a marshmallow.", "F|Hana burned her marshmallow.", "T|Hana saw a shooting star.", "F|Hana told everyone her wish.", "C|When did they go?|in August*|in January|in April", "C|Where did they camp?|at a lake*|on a mountain|in a city", "C|What colour was the tent?|green*|red|yellow", "C|What did they gather?|sticks*|leaves|shells", "C|What did they roast?|marshmallows*|hot dogs|corn", "C|Who showed Hana?|Dad*|Mom|her brother", "C|What did they lie on?|a blanket*|the grass|a boat", "C|What did Hana see?|a shooting star*|an owl|a plane", "C|What did Hana do?|made a wish*|fell asleep|ran inside", "C|What did Hana keep secret?|her wish*|her snack|her name", "B|They set up a green ____.|tent", "B|They gathered ____ for a fire.|sticks", "B|Dad showed her how to roast a ____.|marshmallow", "B|They lay on a ____.|blanket", "B|They looked up at the ____.|sky", "B|Hana saw a shooting ____.|star", "B|She made a ____.|wish"]},
{"title": "The Soccer Team", "text": "Grace joined the Tigers soccer team this spring. At first, she was not very fast, and she missed the ball a lot. Her coach told her to practise passing with a wall at home. Grace practised every day after school. By June, she could pass the ball right to her teammates. In the last game, she helped the Tigers score the winning goal.", "q": ["T|Grace joined the Tigers.", "F|Grace joined in the fall.", "T|At first, Grace missed the ball a lot.", "F|The coach told her to run laps.", "T|Grace practised with a wall.", "F|Grace practised once a week.", "T|Grace improved by June.", "F|The Tigers lost the last game.", "C|What is the team called?|the Tigers*|the Bears|the Hawks", "C|When did Grace join?|this spring*|last winter|this fall", "C|What was hard at first?|she missed the ball*|she got lost|she was sick", "C|What did the coach tell her?|practise passing*|quit|buy new shoes", "C|What did she use at home?|a wall*|a net|a tree", "C|How often did she practise?|every day*|once a month|never", "C|When could she pass well?|by June*|by May|by winter", "C|What happened in the last game?|she helped score the winning goal*|she sat out|it rained", "C|Who did she pass to?|her teammates*|the coach|the other team", "C|What sport does Grace play?|soccer*|hockey|baseball", "B|Grace joined the ____ soccer team.|Tigers", "B|At first, she was not very ____.|fast", "B|She practised passing with a ____.|wall", "B|She practised every day after ____.|school", "B|She could pass to her ____.|teammates", "B|They scored the winning ____.|goal", "B|Her ____ gave her advice.|coach"]},
{"title": "Grandpa’s Old Photos", "text": "On a rainy Sunday, Grandpa showed Amir a box of old photos. In one picture, Grandpa was a boy riding a horse on his family’s farm in Saskatchewan. In another, he was skating on a frozen pond with his brothers. Amir laughed at Grandpa’s funny hat. Grandpa told stories about each picture. Amir said it was the best rainy day ever.", "q": ["T|It was a rainy Sunday.", "F|Grandpa showed Amir a video.", "T|The farm was in Saskatchewan.", "F|Grandpa rode a bike in the photo.", "T|Grandpa skated with his brothers.", "F|The pond was warm.", "T|Amir laughed at a funny hat.", "F|Amir was bored.", "C|What day was it?|Sunday*|Monday|Saturday", "C|What was the weather?|rainy*|sunny|snowy", "C|What did Grandpa show Amir?|old photos*|old toys|a map", "C|Where was the farm?|Saskatchewan*|Ontario|Nova Scotia", "C|What did young Grandpa ride?|a horse*|a tractor|a bike", "C|Where did he skate?|on a frozen pond*|at an arena|on a river", "C|Who skated with him?|his brothers*|his sisters|his dad", "C|What made Amir laugh?|a funny hat*|a dog|a cake", "C|What did Grandpa tell?|stories*|jokes only|nothing", "C|How did Amir feel at the end?|it was the best day*|sad|sleepy", "B|Grandpa showed Amir a ____ of photos.|box", "B|Grandpa was riding a ____.|horse", "B|The farm was in ____.|Saskatchewan", "B|He was skating on a frozen ____.|pond", "B|Amir laughed at a funny ____.|hat", "B|Grandpa told ____ about each picture.|stories", "B|It was the best rainy ____ ever.|day"]},
{"title": "The Food Bank Visit", "text": "Before Thanksgiving, Ms. Choi’s class collected cans for the food bank. Students brought soup, beans, and tuna. They counted 212 cans! Then the class visited the food bank to drop them off. A volunteer named Mr. Grant showed them the shelves and explained how families get food. The students felt proud that they could help their neighbours.", "q": ["T|They collected cans before Thanksgiving.", "F|Ms. Choi’s class collected toys.", "T|Students brought tuna.", "F|They counted 100 cans.", "T|The class visited the food bank.", "F|Mr. Grant is the principal.", "T|Mr. Grant showed them the shelves.", "F|The students felt sad.", "C|When did they collect cans?|before Thanksgiving*|after Christmas|in summer", "C|Who is the teacher?|Ms. Choi*|Ms. Grant|Mr. Lee", "C|What did they collect?|cans*|clothes|books", "C|How many cans did they count?|212*|21|2000", "C|Who showed them around?|Mr. Grant*|Ms. Choi|a farmer", "C|What is Mr. Grant?|a volunteer*|a doctor|a bus driver", "C|What did he explain?|how families get food*|how to cook|how to count", "C|How did the students feel?|proud*|tired|angry", "C|Who did they help?|their neighbours*|their pets|their teachers", "C|Which food was brought?|soup*|ice cream|cake", "B|They collected cans for the food ____.|bank", "B|Students brought soup, beans, and ____.|tuna", "B|They counted 212 ____!|cans", "B|A ____ named Mr. Grant helped.|volunteer", "B|He showed them the ____.|shelves", "B|The students felt ____.|proud", "B|They helped their ____.|neighbours"]},
{"title": "The Big Snowstorm", "text": "A big snowstorm hit Moncton on Tuesday night. In the morning, the snow was as high as Lily’s knees, and school was closed. Lily and her neighbour Tom helped Mrs. Gallant shovel her driveway. Mrs. Gallant thanked them with warm cookies. In the afternoon, the plow came down the street and made a huge snowbank. The kids slid down it all day.", "q": ["T|The storm hit on Tuesday night.", "F|The storm hit Halifax.", "T|School was closed.", "F|The snow was as high as Lily’s head.", "T|Lily helped Mrs. Gallant.", "F|Mrs. Gallant gave them hot soup.", "T|The plow made a snowbank.", "F|The kids built a fort all day.", "C|Where did the storm hit?|Moncton*|Toronto|Calgary", "C|When did it hit?|Tuesday night*|Monday morning|Friday", "C|How high was the snow?|to Lily’s knees*|to her ankles|to her head", "C|Who helped Lily?|her neighbour Tom*|her dad|her teacher", "C|Whose driveway did they shovel?|Mrs. Gallant’s*|their own|the school’s", "C|What did Mrs. Gallant give them?|warm cookies*|money|hot soup", "C|What came in the afternoon?|the plow*|the bus|the mail", "C|What did the plow make?|a huge snowbank*|a hole|a road", "C|What did the kids do?|slid down the snowbank*|went to school|stayed inside", "C|Why was school closed?|the snowstorm*|a holiday|the teacher was sick", "B|A big ____ hit Moncton.|snowstorm", "B|In the morning, school was ____.|closed", "B|They helped shovel her ____.|driveway", "B|She thanked them with warm ____.|cookies", "B|The ____ came down the street.|plow", "B|It made a huge ____.|snowbank", "B|The kids ____ down it all day.|slid"]},
{"title": "Ruby’s Lemonade Stand", "text": "Ruby wanted to buy a new book about dinosaurs. She set up a lemonade stand on her street in Kelowna. She made a sign that said “Lemonade 50¢.” Her first customer was the mail carrier. By noon, Ruby had sold twenty cups. She counted her coins and had ten dollars. Ruby bought the dinosaur book and gave one dollar to the animal shelter.", "q": ["T|Ruby wanted a dinosaur book.", "F|Ruby lives in Victoria.", "T|Her sign said 50¢.", "F|Her first customer was her teacher.", "T|Ruby sold twenty cups by noon.", "F|Ruby had five dollars.", "T|Ruby bought the book.", "F|Ruby kept all the money.", "C|What did Ruby want to buy?|a dinosaur book*|a toy|a bike", "C|Where was her stand?|on her street*|at school|at the park", "C|What city does she live in?|Kelowna*|Ottawa|Halifax", "C|How much was one cup?|50¢*|$1|25¢", "C|Who was the first customer?|the mail carrier*|her mom|a firefighter", "C|How many cups by noon?|twenty*|ten|fifty", "C|How much money did she have?|ten dollars*|two dollars|twenty dollars", "C|What did she buy?|the dinosaur book*|candy|a hat", "C|Where did one dollar go?|the animal shelter*|her piggy bank|the library", "C|What did Ruby make?|a sign*|a cake|a hat", "B|Ruby set up a lemonade ____.|stand", "B|She made a ____.|sign", "B|Her first ____ was the mail carrier.|customer", "B|By ____, she had sold twenty cups.|noon", "B|She counted her ____.|coins", "B|She had ten ____.|dollars", "B|She gave one dollar to the animal ____.|shelter"]},
{"title": "The Robot Kit", "text": "For his birthday, Arjun got a robot kit. The box had wheels, wires, a small motor, and a booklet of steps. Arjun and his big sister followed the steps one by one. When they finished, the robot did not move. They checked every wire and found one that was loose. After they fixed it, the robot rolled across the kitchen floor!", "q": ["T|Arjun got a robot kit.", "F|The kit was for Christmas.", "T|The box had a small motor.", "F|Arjun built it alone.", "T|They followed the steps.", "F|The robot moved right away.", "T|One wire was loose.", "F|The robot rolled across the yard.", "C|When did Arjun get the kit?|his birthday*|Christmas|the first day of school", "C|What was in the box?|wheels and wires*|paint and paper|blocks only", "C|Who helped Arjun?|his big sister*|his dad|his friend", "C|How did they follow the steps?|one by one*|all at once|backwards", "C|What happened first?|the robot did not move*|the robot flew|the robot talked", "C|What did they check?|every wire*|the batteries only|the box", "C|What was the problem?|a loose wire*|a broken wheel|no motor", "C|What did they do?|fixed the wire*|threw it away|bought a new one", "C|Where did the robot roll?|across the kitchen floor*|out the door|up the stairs", "C|What did the booklet have?|steps*|stickers|games", "B|Arjun got a robot ____.|kit", "B|The box had a small ____.|motor", "B|They followed the ____ one by one.|steps", "B|The robot did not ____.|move", "B|They checked every ____.|wire", "B|One wire was ____.|loose", "B|The robot rolled across the kitchen ____.|floor"]},
{"title": "Apple Picking", "text": "On a cool Saturday in September, Zoe’s family went apple picking near Ottawa. The trees were full of red and green apples. Zoe climbed a short ladder to reach the highest branch. She filled her basket with shiny red apples. Dad picked green ones for a pie. At home, they made apple pie together, and the whole house smelled sweet.", "q": ["T|They went on a Saturday.", "F|They went in July.", "T|The orchard was near Ottawa.", "F|The trees had only red apples.", "T|Zoe climbed a short ladder.", "F|Zoe picked green apples.", "T|Dad picked green apples.", "F|They made apple juice.", "C|When did they go?|in September*|in July|in March", "C|What was the weather?|cool*|hot|stormy", "C|Where was the orchard?|near Ottawa*|near Toronto|near Quebec City", "C|What colours were the apples?|red and green*|yellow only|purple", "C|How did Zoe reach high?|a short ladder*|a chair|Dad’s shoulders", "C|What did Zoe pick?|red apples*|green apples|pears", "C|Why did Dad pick green ones?|for a pie*|for juice|for the horse", "C|What did they make at home?|apple pie*|apple sauce|cake", "C|How did the house smell?|sweet*|smoky|sour", "C|What did Zoe fill?|her basket*|her pockets|a box", "B|They went apple ____.|picking", "B|The trees were full of red and green ____.|apples", "B|Zoe climbed a short ____.|ladder", "B|She filled her ____.|basket", "B|Dad picked green ones for a ____.|pie", "B|They made apple pie ____.|together", "B|The whole house smelled ____.|sweet"]},
{"title": "The Kindness Jar", "text": "Mrs. Okafor put an empty jar on her desk. She said, “Every time you see someone being kind, add a marble.” When Omar helped Mia pick up her crayons, a marble went in. When Lucy shared her snack, another went in. In three weeks, the jar was full. The class had a pajama party to celebrate their kindness.", "q": ["T|The jar started empty.", "F|The jar was on the window.", "T|Kind acts earned marbles.", "F|Omar spilled Mia’s crayons.", "T|Lucy shared her snack.", "F|The jar was full in three days.", "T|The class had a party.", "F|It was a pizza party.", "C|Who is the teacher?|Mrs. Okafor*|Mrs. Lee|Mr. Patel", "C|Where was the jar?|on her desk*|on the floor|in the hall", "C|What went in the jar?|marbles*|coins|stickers", "C|When did a marble go in?|when someone was kind*|when someone was late|every hour", "C|What did Omar do?|helped pick up crayons*|shared his lunch|read a book", "C|What did Lucy share?|her snack*|her toy|her pencil", "C|How long until the jar was full?|three weeks*|three days|three months", "C|What kind of party was it?|a pajama party*|a pizza party|a dance", "C|Why did they have a party?|to celebrate kindness*|for a birthday|for winter", "C|Whose crayons fell?|Mia’s*|Omar’s|Lucy’s", "B|She put an empty ____ on her desk.|jar", "B|Add a ____ for kindness.|marble", "B|Omar helped Mia pick up her ____.|crayons", "B|Lucy shared her ____.|snack", "B|In three weeks, the jar was ____.|full", "B|The class had a pajama ____.|party", "B|They celebrated their ____.|kindness"]}
